.page shadow 5 the password database

# DESCRIPTION
`/Hakurei/etc/shadow` holds what passwd(5) leaves out: one line per account, readable only by root (mode 0600), with colon-separated fields of which the first two matter:

    name:hash:19000:0:99999:7:::

The hash field is one of:

@ $gap$_SALT_$_HEX_
    A salted SHA-256: the hex digest of the salt followed by the password. This protects the residents from each other, not from an attacker who has a copy of the file and time to spare, and it makes no claim to more.
@ (empty)
    The account has no password: the empty password is accepted.
@ !
    The account is locked: nothing is accepted. `root` ships this way, so nobody logs in as root; use sudo(1).

The tools that read this file are login(1), su(1), sudo(1), passwd(1), the login screen and the screen lock (through pwcheck(8)). `adduser -L` creates a locked account, `passwd` sets and clears hashes.

With a HUMANVILLAGE volume the file is also kept as `/HumanVillage/.system/etc/shadow` and comes back after a restart (etckeep(8)). FAT stores no permissions, so the kernel presents the folder `.system` as root's, mode 0700, and its files as 0600: nobody else can read the kept copy on this system. Anyone who takes the stick to another computer can.

# SEE ALSO
passwd(5), passwd(1), adduser(8), etckeep(8), accounts(7)
